  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html#the-last-event-id-header\r\n\r\n> 9\\.2\\.4 The \\`Last\\-Event\\-ID\\` header\r\n\r\nThe spec fails to specify how to deal with a `Last-Event-Id` value that is no longer available.\r\n\r\nIf a connection fails, a server will have to buffer events until the client reconnects. At some point the buffer will reach its limits and events will be lost. This is expected. However there is no way specified to notify the client that it missed out on some events because it was disconnected for too long.\r\n\r\nI'd suggest to add a response header specifying the status of the stream;\r\n\r\n* `Sse-Stream-Status: initialized`: new stream, no `Last-Event-Id` was provided (this could also be omitted, but adding it tells the client that the server supports status reporting)\r\n* `Sse-Stream-Status: continue`: resuming stream based on `Last-Event-Id`\r\n* `Sse-Stream-Status: reset`: new stream, provided `Last-Event-Id` is no longer available/unknown\r\n\r\n",
